{"guide":{"questionsToConsider":["What does your refund policy require, such as a time limit or unused condition, and does the form ask for it?","Do you offer store credit or replacements, or only refunds?","Who handles duplicate charges, and can they act without the customer returning anything?","Do you need the item back before refunding, and how will you send return instructions?"],"howToUseResponses":"Check each request against your refund policy using the order date and condition answers, and approve the clear cases quickly. Damage photos are worth passing to your supplier or courier when the same fault keeps coming up. Export to CSV monthly and count requests by reason: a rise in items that weren't as expected usually points to a product page that needs better photos or wording.","customizeSteps":["Edit the reasons and resolutions so they match your refund policy.","Add your return window or conditions to the greeting so people know them before they start.","Link the form from order confirmation emails and your returns page."],"faqs":[{"q":"What should a refund request form include?","a":"The customer's email, the order number, the date, the reason for the refund, any evidence such as photos, the condition of the item, and whether they want a refund, credit or replacement."},{"q":"Should customers upload photos for a refund?","a":"For damaged or faulty items, yes. This form only asks for photos when the customer says the item arrived damaged, so nobody else is asked for them."},{"q":"Can I offer store credit instead of a refund?","a":"Yes. The form asks what the customer would prefer, and you can edit the options to match what your policy allows."},{"q":"How do I track refund requests?","a":"Every request lands in your dashboard with its reason and order number, and you can export them to CSV to track them alongside your orders."}]},"doc":{"schemaVersion":9,"title":"Refund request","description":"Refund requests with the evidence your team needs, collected once.","blocks":[{"id":"blk_refundre00","ref":"welcome","title":"Let's sort this out. First, a few details about the order.","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"buttonLabel":"Start","type":"welcome"},{"id":"blk_refundre01","ref":"email","title":"Which email did you use for the order?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"email","unique":false,"businessOnly":false,"allowedDomains":[],"verify":false},{"id":"blk_refundre02","ref":"order_reference","title":"Your order or invoice number","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"short_text","unique":false,"minLength":0,"maxLength":60},{"id":"blk_refundre03","ref":"order_date","title":"Roughly when did you order?","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"date","disablePast":false,"dateFormat":"YYYY-MM-DD","includeTime":false,"timeStepMinutes":30,"timeMin":"09:00","timeMax":"18:00"},{"id":"blk_refundre04","ref":"amount","title":"How much did you pay?","description":"An estimate is fine.","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"number","unique":false,"min":0,"integerOnly":false},{"id":"blk_refundre05","ref":"reason","title":"Why are you asking for a refund?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_it_arrived_damaged","label":"It arrived damaged or faulty","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_it_never_arrived","label":"It never arrived","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_i_was_charged","label":"I was charged twice","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_it_wasn_t","label":"It wasn't what I expected","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_i_changed_my","label":"I changed my mind","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_refundre06","ref":"damage_photos","title":"Photos of the damage","description":"One of the item and one 